      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To improve your document's structural score without increasing \"scroll-fatigue,\" you can use more meaningful subheadings and bullet points to group related actions logically.\n\nHere is the expanded \"Getting Started\" guide for the CloudScale API organized by concept:\n\n### Prerequisites\n*   Ensure your environment has an active API key.\n*   Verify your account has the necessary permissions for service creation.\n*   Install the official SDK for your preferred language (Node.js, Python, or Go).\n\n### Authentication Setup\n*   Locate your active credentials in the CloudScale Dashboard.\n*   Copy your secret key or access token securely.\n*   Configure your client library to use Basic auth or pass the token in headers automatically.\n\n### Creating a Service Identity\n*   Select a unique name for your new microservice instance.\n*   Define the version tag to ensure backward compatibility.\n*   Submit a request to the `/v1/services` endpoint with your specified parameters.\n\n### Retrieving Configuration Data\n*   Make a GET request to list all current configurations.\n*   Filter results by environment tag (e.g., `prod` or `stage`).\n*   Extract the service URL and routing rules returned in the",
      "source": "target",
